    {
      "id": "claim_9a8a113778b64ec0b3629464fee0328b",
      "statement": "OpenWiki keeps two in-memory startup snapshots — the shell's values for managed keys (captureShellEnv/getShellEnvValue, idempotent so the first call wins) and the saved file's values (savedEnvAtStartup/getSavedEnvValue) — both never persisted or logged, so the setup wizard can distinguish shell overrides from saved config.",
